.TH NETIFYD 8
.SH NAME
@PACKAGE_TARNAME@ \- The @PACKAGE_NAME@ v@PACKAGE_VERSION@
.SH DESCRIPTION
The @PACKAGE_NAME@ (The Agent) is a high-performance, multi-threaded passive network traffic analyzer that leverages deep-packet inspection (DPI) to identify network protocols and applications in near realtime. It is designed to provide comprehensive network visibility by capturing traffic from multiple network capture sources simultaneously.

Key features and capabilities include:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBProtocol & Application Detection\fR: Utilizing the nDPI engine, the Agent accurately classifies thousands of protocols and applications in real-time, including support for encrypted traffic analysis.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMetadata Extraction\fR: Beyond simple classification, the Agent extracts rich flow metadata, including network statistics, connection durations, protocol-specific details, and flow risk analysis.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDevice Identification\fR: Analyzes traffic patterns to identify and categorize devices on the network, distinguishing between IoT devices, workstations, mobile devices, and more.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFlexible Data Export\fR: Classification and flow data are JSON-encoded and can be exported to local files, served over UNIX or TCP sockets, or pushed to remote endpoints via HTTP/S POST requests.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPlugin Architecture\fR: Supports a modular plugin system that allows for extending functionality, such as custom data sinks, integration with local databases, or specialized analysis modules.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInformatics Integration\fR: Optionally integrates with the Netify Informatics cloud platform for advanced machine-learning analysis, historical reporting, event notifications, and long-term storage.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBActive Control Support\fR: On supported platforms, the Agent can be configured to take an active role in network policing, bandwidth shaping, and policy enforcement based on real-time DPI results.

The Agent is built with C++17 and optimized for efficiency, making it suitable for deployment on a wide range of hardware, from embedded gateways and IoT devices to high-performance servers.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-provision\fR
.IR

.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
\fB\-\-enable/disable-sink\fR | \fB\-\-enable/disable-informatics\fR
.IR

.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-status\fR
.IR

.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-dump-all\fR | \fB\-\-dump-apps/protos/categories/risks\fR | \fB\-\-lookup-ip\fR=\fIADDRESS\fR
.IR

.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-uuidgen\fR
.IR

.B @PACKAGE_TARNAME@
[\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-debug-ndpi\fR]
[\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-debug-curl\fR]
[\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-debug-log\fR=\fIFILENAME\fR]
[\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-debug-flow-expression\fR=\fIEXPR\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-debug-flow-log\fR=\fIFILENAME\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-disable-conntrack\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-disable-netlink\fR]
[\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-remain-in-foreground\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-replay-delay\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR=\fICONFIG\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-uuid\fR=\fIUUID\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-ndpi-config\fR=\fIFILENAME\fR]
[\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-export-json\fR=\fIFILENAME\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR=\fISECONDS\fR]
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-internal\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR [capture device opts...] [\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-internal\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR]...
\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-external\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR [capture device opts...] [\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-external\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR]...
.IR

.B Capture device options:
[\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-device-address\fR=\fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-device-filter\fR=\fIBPF\fR]
[\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-device-peer\fR=\fIINTERFACE\fR]
.IR
.SH OPTIONS
.BR \-p ", " \-\-provision
.TP
Generate a new client UUID if one hasn't already been set.  Display the URL used to provision this Agent.
.TP
.BR \-\-enable-informatics ", " \-\-disable-informatics
Automatically configure and enable the plugins required for Netify Informatics.  When enabled, flow metadata and DPI detection information will be uploaded to Netify Informatics for further processing and analysis.  A
.UR https://www.netify.ai/products/netify-informatics
Netify Informatics Subscription
.UE
is required.  This option is disabled by default.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status
Display the latest service status.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-dump-all
Display the current protocol and service ID list (all protocols and applications).
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-apps ", " \-\-dump-protos
Display the current application or protocol list.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-categories ", " \-\-dump-category " " \fITYPE\fR
Display application and protocol categories.  The \fITYPE\fR can be either 'application' or 'protocol'.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-risks
Display flow security risks.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-sort-by-tag
Sort dump entries by tag (default: sort by ID).
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-with-categories
When dumping applications or protocols, also include category information.
.TP
.BR \-\-export-apps
Export the application list to stdout in JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-\-export-legacy
Export the application list to stdout in legacy (nDPI) format.
.TP
.BR \-\-lookup-ip=\fIADDRESS\fR
Perform application and category query by IP address.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-uuidgen
Generate a client UUID.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
When running in foreground mode, enabling verbose mode will display each flow detection as they complete.  Specify multiple times to increase verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose-flag " " \fIFLAG\fR
In debug mode, display or hide specified flow event types: [no-]event-dpi-new, [no-]event-dpi-update, or [no-]event-dpi-complete.  Can be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug mode.  Remain in the foreground and emit debug messages.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-debug-ndpi
In debug mode, display nDPI debug messages when enabled (compile-time).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-debug-curl
In debug mode, display debug output from libCURL.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-debug-log=\fIFILENAME\fR
In debug mode, write debug messages to \fIFILENAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-debug-flow-expression=\fIEXPR\fR
In debug mode, filter flow detections by expression.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-debug-flow-log=\fIFILENAME\fR
In debug mode, write flow debug messages to \fIFILENAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remain-in-foreground
Remain in the foreground, do not daemonize.
.TP
.BR \-\-allow-unprivileged
Allow executing the Agent as a non-root user.
.TP
.BR \-\-run-without-sources
Continue running with no capture sources.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-restart
Prevent the Agent from being restarted.
.TP
.BR \-\-enable-coredumps
Enable coredumps.
.TP
.BR \-\-force-reset
Reset global sink configuration options.
.TP
.BR \-\-enable-plugin ", " \-\-disable-plugin ", " \-\-edit-plugin " " \fIPLUGIN\fR
Enable, disable, or edit the configuration for the specified \fIPLUGIN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-disable-conntrack
Disable connection tracking support.  This option will disable IP NAT detection for flows captured from external interfaces.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-disable-netlink
Disable netlink support.  This option will disable the detection of IP address and routing changes.  The address and routing configuration for an interface must be supplied using the \-\-device-address=\fIADDRESS\fR option (described below).
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-device-address=\fIADDRESS\fR
For interfaces receiving mirrored traffic, or when netlink is disabled or unavailable, use this to specify the addresses local to the previous interface (-I, or -E) parameter.  Can be specified more than once for multiple addresses.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-device-filter=\fIBPF\fR
Interface/device option: attach a BPF filter expression to the interface.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-device-peer=\fIINTERFACE\fR
Interface/device option: associate the interface with a peer (e.g., PPPoE interface, pppX).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config=\fICONFIG\fR
Specify an alternate configuration file.  Default: /etc/@PACKAGE_TARNAME@.conf
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-uuid=\fIUUID\fR
Specify a client serial number (UUID).  Used for device identification with Netify Informatics.  Normally, the auto-generated client UUID is used for this purpose.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-ndpi-config=\fIFILENAME\fR
Specify an alternate legacy (nDPI) application configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-export-json=\fIFILENAME\fR
JSON encode flow and application state and write it to this file every update interval.  \fBNOTE:\fR the \fIjson_export\fR option must be enabled in @PACKAGE_TARNAME@.conf(5) for this payload to be written.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval=\fISECONDS\fR
Specify the update interval in seconds.
.TP
.BR \-\-capture-delay=\fISECONDS\fR
Wait \fISECONDS\fR before starting capture thread(s).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore-interface-configs
Don't load capture interface configuration file entries.  Only configure capture interfaces set using command-line options.
.TP
.BR \-\-disable-auto-flow-expiry
Don't auto-expire flows on exit.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-internal=\fIINTERFACE\fR
Capture packets on this internal (LAN) interface.  Can be specified more than once for multiple interfaces.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-external=\fIINTERFACE\fR
Capture packets on this external (WAN) interface.  Can be specified more than once for multiple interfaces.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replay-delay
Simulate packet-to-packet arrival times in offline playback mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-thread-capture-base=\fIOFFSET\fR
Specify a thread affinity base or offset for capture threads.
.TP
.BR \-\-thread-detection-base=\fIOFFSET\fR
Specify a thread affinity base or offset for detection (DPI) threads.
.TP
.BR \-\-thread-detection-cores=\fICOUNT\fR
Specify the number of detection (DPI) threads to start.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-hash-file=\fIFILENAME\fR
Calculate and display the SHA1 hash of \fIFILENAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and features.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGHUP
Reload the run-time configuration and capture threads.
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM ", " SIGPWR
Initiate a clean shutdown of the Agent.  Send twice to shutdown immediately.
.TP
.BR SIGUSR1
Save the DNS hint and flow hash caches to disk.  If Netify API updates are enabled, force an update.
.TP
.BR SIGUSR2
Toggle debug logging between the configured debug log file and stderr.
